>
> You'd also probably have to take your gloves off.

   On the contrary, I'd think taking your gloves off would only increase
the chances of getting a painful splinter (and abusing wisdom!). The
way I know the superstition, you don't have to knock on wood with your
bare hand --- it doesn't even have to be your hand at all; it could be
your foot, a hammer, whatever.

   #rubbing is a poor synonym for "knocking" anyway; surely if any "knock
on wood" YANI were to be implemented, it would involve using the "knock"
spell...

   You see here a +0 elven dagger.
   Zap which spell? knock
   Which direction?
   You feel lucky!

Not that I'm suggesting that particular usage; it's way too obscure a
combination to be fair. But that's the pun we should be thinking about,
not #rubbing.

   Maybe using "knock" on a wood golem...?  Heck, maybe just hitting a
wood golem in melee should have a chance of fixing bad luck.  Hey,
that's a good idea!

